session:pr222Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Adds SPARQL 1.1 BASE <iri> prologue parsing (alongside PREFIX) and relative-IRI resolution against it, per §4.1 / RFC 3986. ParserContext gains a base: Option<String> field: the effective base IRI. A caller can set it to a natural default (e.g. a query file's own path); an in-query BASE <iri> directive overrides that default for the rest of the query, and is itself resolved against whatever base was already in effect (so a relative BASE can extend a caller-supplied default). Resolution is centralized in a single choke point (parse_iri_ref/parse_iri_ref_resolved in sparql_parser/src/lib.rs), which every <...> reference in the grammar goes through: triple patterns, PREFIX/BASE IRIs, GRAPH/FROM clauses, datatype IRIs, function names. Resolution logic uses oxiri (promoted from a transitive to a direct dependency of sparql_parser), the same crate turtle's underlying oxttl parser already uses for @base — no hand-rolled RFC 3986 logic. No-base fallback decision When there is genuinely no base available (no BASE directive, no caller-supplied default), a relative IRI reference is kept verbatim rather than raising a parse error. This deliberately differs from turtle::parse_turtle's stricter no-base behavior (which hard-errors on any non-absolute IRI, since oxttl/oxiri's Iri::parse rejects relative references outright when no base is set)." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:222 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr222 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
